{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/467478-anything-about-sidereals-yet","id":467478,"title":"Anything about Sidereals yet?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-03T09:27:38-07:00","id":467478,"title":"Anything about Sidereals yet?","content":"I'm just curious, for 3rd edition, have we gotten any real information about Sidereals? I know I've read that the general idea with the charm set is it's canonically closed but the dev team's not against adding &quot;They were always there&quot; charms later (Something I fully support), but I think that's the only real mention of them I've seen.<br /> <br /> Has there been even the slightest tidbit of a hint about other systems for them; Arcane Fate, Astrology, that sorta thing? Or are they likely too far down the line to have anything just yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T09:54:48-07:00","id":467540,"title":"","content":"We don't have a lot of hard details about Sidereal mechanics; I think it likely is too far out for the devs to want to commit themselves, given how tricky Sidereals can be to get right. You can read some of what we've heard about their Charmset in its section of the What We Know Wiki, <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Charms#Sidereal_Charms\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. It's mostly reiterations, expositions, and pontifications on the closed Charmset, though.<br /> <br /> We have learned a bit more on them in a more general sense, though. <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Sidereals\" target=\"_blank\">Their section</a> on the What We Know Wiki isn't as expansive as some others at the moment, but does touch lightly on some mechanical mentions and give some setting and fluff discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T10:42:49-07:00","id":467571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/467478-anything-about-sidereals-yet?p=467540#post467540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't have a lot of hard details about Sidereal mechanics; I think it likely is too far out for the devs to want to commit themselves, given how tricky Sidereals can be to get right. You can read some of what we've heard about their Charmset in its section of the What We Know Wiki, <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Charms#Sidereal_Charms\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. It's mostly reiterations, expositions, and pontifications on the closed Charmset, though.<br /> <br /> We have learned a bit more on them in a more general sense, though. <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Sidereals\" target=\"_blank\">Their section</a> on the What We Know Wiki isn't as expansive as some others at the moment, but does touch lightly on some mechanical mentions and give some setting and fluff discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah I had seen the wiki a while back but hadn't realized there was a Sidereal section.<br /> <br /> At least they noted Astrology will be easier and less costly, which I like. I also noticed the wiki said something about another addition to their power set they won't get into yet, which has me wondering. Overall, what little's been said sounds promising, though I'll admit I'm new to Exalted overall, so have trouble gauging what should be prioritized as I lack the experience so far.<br /> <br /> One thing I'm iffy about though is that they might have some limit on evocations? Still, looking forward to learning more, as a lot's unsaid so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T10:44:10-07:00","id":467576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/467478-anything-about-sidereals-yet?p=467540#post467540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't have a lot of hard details about Sidereal mechanics; I think it likely is too far out for the devs to want to commit themselves, given how tricky Sidereals can be to get right.</div> </div> </div> </div>If nothing else, I think that the devs would have to actively and purposefully give Sidereals shit mechanics for them to be worse than 2e Sids. Of course, saying &quot;Better than 2e Sidereals&quot; is putting the bar so low that you actually have to dig down several feet.<br /> <br /> Generally, here's the goals I would want for 3e Sidereals:<br /> <br /> Mechanics that reflect the current edition of the game. This should go without saying, but see 2e Sidereals.<br /> Enough breadth in the Charm trees that you can actually branch off and/or have different builds<br /> Not picking Occult and/or Martial Arts doesn't make you an idiot<br /> Astrology that's fun and interesting to use, including a discussion on the impact it has on the setting (&quot;Okay, so I gave the East -1 TN on farming rolls. So, what does that <i>mean</i>?&quot;)<br /> NO FUCKING PARADOX<br /> Not being required to pick Occult and/or Martial Arts<br /> Less Destiny-Knitting Entanglement, more Celestial Drifter's Panoply<br /> More game-able Charms in general, actually<br /> No Charms that require multiple Sidereals; Charms that get <i>better</i> with multiple Sidereals are okay<br /> Less feeling like every character needs to take Occult and/or Martial Arts<br /> SMA that's actually usable in average game, both in accessibility and in not being &quot;Holy fuckballs, Creation Slaying Oblivion Kick no wai.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...I'll probably think of more, I'm sure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:09:36-07:00","id":467626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/467478-anything-about-sidereals-yet?p=467576#post467576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not picking Occult and/or Martial Arts doesn't make you an idiot<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just so we're clear, Coik, you mean not picking them as Auspicious/Favored, rather than &quot;not taking any dots&quot;, yes?<br /> <br /> There is I think a very strong argument that if you're a non-Ronin Sidereal, you should be &quot;required&quot; (in the sense that you get them &quot;for free&quot; but chargen is balanced around those &quot;free&quot; dots) to have a certain number of dots in those abilities and others, the same way that a Dynast is required to have a broad array of dots in certain abilities to reflect the fact that those are the bare minimum you are expected to learn as a functional member of that particular society.<br /> <br /> I can't see Sidereal Sifu's clearing people for active duty without hitting what they consider to be benchmarks of minimal competency.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:17:19-07:00","id":467633,"title":"","content":"Or slapping them with training effects and telling them to deal with the xp debt, then moving on to more important matters, like how they'll be useful minions to their sifu by procuring an invitation to Venus' next hottub ballroom dancing event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:18:30-07:00","id":467634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/467478-anything-about-sidereals-yet?p=467576#post467576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If nothing else, I think that the devs would have to actively and purposefully give Sidereals shit mechanics for them to be worse than 2e Sids. Of course, saying &quot;Better than 2e Sidereals&quot; is putting the bar so low that you actually have to dig down several feet.<br /> <br /> Generally, here's the goals I would want for 3e Sidereals:<br /> <br /> Mechanics that reflect the current edition of the game. This should go without saying, but see 2e Sidereals.<br /> Enough breadth in the Charm trees that you can actually branch off and/or have different builds<br /> Not picking Occult and/or Martial Arts doesn't make you an idiot<br /> Astrology that's fun and interesting to use, including a discussion on the impact it has on the setting (&quot;Okay, so I gave the East -1 TN on farming rolls. So, what does that <i>mean</i>?&quot;)<br /> NO FUCKING PARADOX<br /> Not being required to pick Occult and/or Martial Arts<br /> Less Destiny-Knitting Entanglement, more Celestial Drifter's Panoply<br /> More game-able Charms in general, actually<br /> No Charms that require multiple Sidereals; Charms that get <i>better</i> with multiple Sidereals are okay<br /> Less feeling like every character needs to take Occult and/or Martial Arts<br /> SMA that's actually usable in average game, both in accessibility and in not being &quot;Holy fuckballs, Creation Slaying Oblivion Kick no wai.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...I'll probably think of more, I'm sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>3e Sidereals: You get Paradox every scene in which you didn't use Occult or Martial Arts. There's a charm to reduce your Paradox, but you need at least three Sidereals working together to use it, and they all have to share a Motivation. When your Paradox breaks, everyone in the same Direction as you gets +1 TN to their Lore rolls for a season because all the paradoxes make it harder to know anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:24:18-07:00","id":467641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/467478-anything-about-sidereals-yet?p=467576#post467576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If nothing else, I think that the devs would have to actively and purposefully give Sidereals shit mechanics for them to be worse than 2e Sids. Of course, saying &quot;Better than 2e Sidereals&quot; is putting the bar so low that you actually have to dig down several feet.<br /> <br /> Generally, here's the goals I would want for 3e Sidereals:<br /> <br /> Mechanics that reflect the current edition of the game. This should go without saying, but see 2e Sidereals.<br /> Enough breadth in the Charm trees that you can actually branch off and/or have different builds<br /> Not picking Occult and/or Martial Arts doesn't make you an idiot<br /> Astrology that's fun and interesting to use, including a discussion on the impact it has on the setting (&quot;Okay, so I gave the East -1 TN on farming rolls. So, what does that <i>mean</i>?&quot;)<br /> NO FUCKING PARADOX<br /> Not being required to pick Occult and/or Martial Arts<br /> Less Destiny-Knitting Entanglement, more Celestial Drifter's Panoply<br /> More game-able Charms in general, actually<br /> No Charms that require multiple Sidereals; Charms that get <i>better</i> with multiple Sidereals are okay<br /> Less feeling like every character needs to take Occult and/or Martial Arts<br /> SMA that's actually usable in average game, both in accessibility and in not being &quot;Holy fuckballs, Creation Slaying Oblivion Kick no wai.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...I'll probably think of more, I'm sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you forgot to mention that there should be less of a need to focus on Occult and martial arts?<br /> <br /> More seriously, I'll admit when I first heard about Astrology from the friend of mine that recently got me into Exalted, I loved the idea of it, but then I read the complexity of it and read about how it rarely is worth much in game in 2e, and it made me sad. So Astrology is high on my list for what I want to see in 3e.<br /> <br /> That and a new unique mechanic for Sidereals sounds good, as was mentioned, heh.<br /> <br /> As a note, the 'you need additional Viziers' charms were basically nixed in the 2.5, right? So I can't imagine them bringing them back since it's the same team, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:31:25-07:00","id":467674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/467478-anything-about-sidereals-yet?p=467571#post467571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'm iffy about though is that they might have some limit on evocations? Still, looking forward to learning more, as a lot's unsaid so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>My read on it from a gameplay perspective is that it might actually work out better for them. The EX3 Team has mentioned keeping an eye on synergy and interactions between different parts of the system a lot more than in the past for the new edition. Through their native Charms and to the end of a unique play space, Sidereals can get at odd capabilities that nobody else really has, while also not possessing some things other splats take for granted. Part of the reasoning for this is that having those together in one Charmset could be unbalancing. The same idea could carry over into Evocations: combining some of the powers Evocations can grant with some of their more unconventional Charms could create some imbalance, meaning they'd either need to lack that Evocation access or lack their more unique capacities. If it came down to that decision, I know I'd take &quot;keep their native unique capacities&quot; every time.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that they're only missing out on Evocations if having low capacity with them is framed as a net loss. As Coik notes above, SMA now being in range for an average game probably makes up for it, anyway. I mean, at the Essence ratings that the vast majority of SMAs needed to master them? They were basically an option that Sidereals <i>technically had</i>, but were very unlikely to get to realize. Even aside from the copious amounts of broken all over most SMAs. So they're moving from 2e's &quot;would mostly not really be able to get SMA, for reasons of stats or ST fiat&quot; to EX3's &quot;will be able to get SMA, something in the way of Evocations, and probably a more expansive Charmset.&quot; At least at this point, I think they've got nothing but gains. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/467478-anything-about-sidereals-yet?p=467576#post467576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If nothing else, I think that the devs would have to actively and purposefully give Sidereals shit mechanics for them to be worse than 2e Sids. Of course, saying &quot;Better than 2e Sidereals&quot; is putting the bar so low that you actually have to dig down several feet.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, true. Also, nice summation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:33:32-07:00","id":467676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/467478-anything-about-sidereals-yet?p=467626#post467626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just so we're clear, Coik, you mean not picking them as Auspicious/Favored, rather than &quot;not taking any dots&quot;, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yar. I'm referring to how the closed (and <i>small</i>) nature of the Sidereal Charmset overwhelmingly incentivizes picking Occult and Martial Arts as Favored/Caste, because on a long enough XP line they become your only growth potential. Hell, think the earliest I've seen it happen was around 50XP, because the player didn't want to dip too deeply into Charms in abilities outside his character concept.<br /> <br /> I don't have an issue with Bureau Sid/Dynast DB ability minimums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:35:54-07:00","id":467679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/467478-anything-about-sidereals-yet?p=467674#post467674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My read on it from a gameplay perspective is that it might actually work out better for them. The EX3 Team has mentioned keeping an eye on synergy and interactions between different parts of the system a lot more than in the past for the new edition. Through their native Charms and to the end of a unique play space, Sidereals can get at odd capabilities that nobody else really has, while also not possessing some things other splats take for granted. Part of the reasoning for this is that having those together in one Charmset could be unbalancing. The same idea could carry over into Evocations: combining some of the powers Evocations can grant with some of their more unconventional Charms could create some imbalance, meaning they'd either need to lack that Evocation access or lack their more unique capacities. If it came down to that decision, I know I'd take &quot;keep their native unique capacities&quot; every time.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that they're only missing out on Evocations if having low capacity with them is framed as a net loss. As Coik notes above, SMA now being in range for an average game probably makes up for it, anyway. I mean, at the Essence ratings that the vast majority of SMAs needed to master them? They were basically an option that Sidereals <i>technically had</i>, but were very unlikely to get to realize. Even aside from the copious amounts of broken all over most SMAs. So they're moving from 2e's &quot;would mostly not really be able to get SMA, for reasons of stats or ST fiat&quot; to EX3's &quot;will be able to get SMA, something in the way of Evocations, and probably a more expansive Charmset.&quot; At least at this point, I think they've got nothing but gains. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. Like I said, I only have limited actual experience and a lot of forum browsing, re;Sidereals, despite them theoretically being my favorite Exalts. So, yes, I agree, if their unique capabilities are made in a way to be interesting and useful and in trade they get less ability to use evocations (and of course are charm locked), I'd be perfectly fine with that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}